spec:
  grid: 11x11, always fixed
  structure: |
    3x3 macro grid of 3x3 tiles separated by 2 grey (5) full rows and columns
    at positions 3 and 7, giving tile bands [0-3), [4-7), [8-11).
  tiles:
    count: 9 (3x3 macro grid)
    cell_fill: 1-4 non-black pixels per tile; each pixel a distinct color [observed except test_0 has one dup]
    colors: drawn from {1,2,3,6,7,8,9} (never grey=5, never yellow=4 except source)
  source_tile:
    exactly one tile contains exactly one yellow (4) pixel
    non-black count: 3-4
    yellow is part of the tile content (not overlaid on another color)
    source_tile != destination_tile (src macro position != yellow local position)
  destination:
    determined by yellow pixel's local (row, col) within the source tile
    that local coordinate selects the macro (row, col) of the destination slot
  output: grey separator grid preserved; destination tile gets source tile content; all other tiles cleared to black

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Create 11x11 black grid. Place grey separators at rows/cols {3, 7}.
    2. Pick destination slot (dst_br, dst_bc) uniformly from 0-2.
    3. Generate destination tile content - a 3x3 tile with 3-4 non-black pixels
       using colors from {1,2,3,6,7,8,9} (all distinct within tile).
       Exactly one pixel must be yellow (4); its local position (lr, lc) must
       satisfy (lr, lc) != (dst_br, dst_bc) so source != destination.
    4. Place tile into destination slot. This is the output.
    5. Build input - source tile at macro (lr, lc) is a copy of the destination tile.
    6. Fill remaining 8 tiles with random 1-4 non-black pixels each, colors
       from {1,2,3,6,7,8,9} (no yellow=4), each pixel a distinct color.
    7. Place all 9 tiles + grey separators to form the 11x11 input grid.
