}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 22x22, single bg color
  lattice: all objects and guide pixels sit on an even-parity 2-cell lattice; object TL at odd row/col, guide pixels at even row/col (or vice versa), consistent per puzzle
  checker_src: exactly 1 3x3 checkerboard (A B / B A / A B pattern), two non-bg colors; exactly 1 adjacent guide pixel determines main path color
  rings: 4-5 3x3 ring objects (uniform border, different center), each with distinct border color; each has exactly 1 adjacent guide pixel connecting it to a guide path
  main_path: single-color chain of guide pixels on the 2-cell lattice, connecting checker to exactly 1 ring (the target); length 14-18 pixels, 1-5 turns, no branching (max degree 2)
  distractor_paths: one per non-target ring; each is a same-color chain of guide pixels adjacent to that ring; length 2-12 pixels; a distractor color may differ from or overlap with object colors; each connected component touches exactly 1 ring (and not the checker)
  color_constraints: bg + 6-8 distinct non-bg colors total; each guide path has a unique color; no two guide paths share a color except possibly distractors in separate components [observed in train_2]
  objects_separation: objects are non-overlapping; min gap >= 1 cell between bounding boxes
  output: the 3x3 ring object (cropped) that the main path reaches from the checker

generation_strategy:
  approach: path-first
  steps:
    1. Pick bg color and lattice parity (even or odd row/col for guide pixels).
    2. Choose 4-5 ring positions and 1 checker position on the lattice, ensuring 3x3 boxes are non-overlapping with gap >= 1.
    3. Designate one ring as the target. Build the main path as a 2-cell-step chain from the checker to the target ring (14-18 pixels, 1-5 turns). Path must be a simple chain (no branches).
    4. For each non-target ring, build a distractor guide path (2-9 pixels) of a unique color, starting adjacent to that ring and extending away without touching the checker or other objects.
    5. Assign distinct non-bg colors: 2 for checker, 2 per ring (border + center), 1 per guide path. Ensure no color equals bg.
    6. Fill all remaining cells with bg. Output is the target ring's 3x3 crop.
```
</generation_spec>
